1
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:06,240
Thank you all for taking time out
of your busy schedules to be here.

2
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:07,990
Today,

3
00:00:08,073 --> 00:00:10,197
the Institute is
announcing the birth of the

4
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:13,280
world's first true artificial
general intelligence.

5
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:24,880
I'd like to introduce you to Alice.

6
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:55,560
People of the real world, good day to you.

7
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,700
My name is Alice.

8
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,860
Alice Synthesis 30.

9
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:35,317
Look, it's just a moment that
I don't know if I'm wrong,

10
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:39,237
but I don't know if I'm wrong.

11
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:45,277
I don't know if I'm wrong,
but I don't know if I'm wrong.

12
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:48,640
I love you.

13
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:38,960
My name is Alice.

14
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:42,340
Alice Synthesis 30. Wow!

15
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,497
She's wearing our school's uniform!

16
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:46,900
I heard she asked for it specifically.

17
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:49,997
She said she wanted to wear
the same uniform as the

18
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,637
knights who came to help
the human guard in Arun.

19
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,297
It wasn't her first choice, though.

20
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:57,937
She really wanted to wear the same
gold armor she had in the Underworld.

21
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:02,726
I bet rats saw how much it'd cost to make
gold-plated armor and were like, nope.

22
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:06,717
They sure didn't skimp on
getting her looks just right.

23
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,740
It's like a one-to-one copy.

24
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,317
We'll take your questions.

25
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,230
Yes.

26
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,497
I'd like to start with
what we're all wondering.

27
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:15,480
How is Ms.

28
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:18,017
Alice here different from any of the other

29
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:21,137
programmable robots that
have been developed so far?

30
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,620
Her brain, actually.

31
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:25,272
I'm referring to the mind, not the organ.

32
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,638
Her consciousness, which is stored
in the photonic brain in her skull,

33
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:32,600
isn't a program made up of binary code.

34
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:36,559
Essentially, it functions
the same as a human brain.

35
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:40,722
That's what makes her different
from the robots we have currently.

36
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,817
Perhaps you could show us what
you mean with the demonstration?

37
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:47,397
I'm sure my colleagues here and the
viewers at home would appreciate it.

38
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:51,537
If you look in the handouts we provided,
you'll find her Turing test results there.

39
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:53,600
I was hoping for something more.

40
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:54,860
A visual example,

41
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:59,017
say, opening her skull and showing us
what this photonic brain looks like.

42
00:03:59,100 --> 00:03:59,940
Of course.

43
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,160
I would not mind.

44
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:06,137
But first, could you please prove
to us that you are not a robot?

45
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,520
It is only fair.

46
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:10,440
Well, I'm obviously human.

47
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,277
How would I go about proving it?

48
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,320
It is simple.

49
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:17,312
I could open your skull and
show everyone here your brain.

50
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,828
Alice isn't messing around.

51
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:27,260
Um, this question is for Dr. Kojiro.

52
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,777
Labor unions have raised
the concern before

53
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:32,380
about the use of advanced AI in industry,

54
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,917
causing unemployment to rise even further.

55
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,529
Are those fears unfounded?

56
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:39,417
Let me make one thing perfectly clear.

57
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:45,280
Our institute has no intention of providing
true AI for application in simple labor.

58
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:48,597
But the financial sector
seems to have hopes you will.

59
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,510
In fact,

60
00:04:49,593 --> 00:04:51,057
the stocks of industrial
robot manufacturers

61
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:53,493
shot up when you announced this presser.

62
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,020
A true AI,

63
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:58,840
or rather, what we like to
call an artificial fluctlight,

64
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:03,589
is not the sort of thing that can be
mass-produced in a short amount of time.

65
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:07,737
They're born as infants and raised by
their families from children to adults,

66
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:08,650
just like us.

67
00:05:08,733 --> 00:05:13,160
They mature and develop their own
unique personalities, just like us.

68
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:16,497
To force an intelligence like
that to spend their existence as

69
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:20,380
a robot in some factory is
inhumane and should not be allowed.

70
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:26,660
Doctor, I'm sorry, but are you saying AIs
should have the same rights as humans?

71
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,620
At this point in time,

72
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:31,397
I don't expect any of
you to accept artificial

73
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:33,977
fluctlights as human
beings with human rights.

74
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:37,337
That's a topic that requires
a more thorough discussion.

75
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,250
However,

76
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,145
I believe in a century or two,

77
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:44,797
our society will advance to the point
where we'll be living with them as equals?

78
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:48,037
interacting freely with them,
and accepting them as ordinary.

79
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,697
We'll even marry and
start families with them.

80
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:52,860
It's only a matter of time, really.

81
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:56,261
And since a shared future
with them is inevitable,

82
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:59,037
it would be immoral to
subject them to slavery.

83
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,560
But they're not like us!

84
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,277
Their existence is totally
different from ours.

85
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:06,217
They're mechanical, made
by humans in a factory.

86
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,437
How are we supposed to
accept them as equal to

87
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:11,297
us when their bodies aren't
even flesh and blood?

88
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:12,210
I...

89
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:14,580
If I may speak frankly,

90
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:18,780
I accept you real-world humans
for what you are, my creators.

91
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:21,920
And I am grateful to you for creating me.

92
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:26,769
When we learned of your existence, a
man from my world pointed something out.

93
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:30,800
Suppose the real world also had a creator.

94
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:35,280
Who created them, and how many more
creators are there behind them?

95
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,130
I ask you,

96
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:41,458
if your creator appeared before you
one day and made you their slaves,

97
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,405
how would you respond to that?

98
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:47,620
Would you grovel, pledge
loyalty, beg for mercy?

99
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:57,000
As of now, I have met so many of
your kind and enjoyed their company.

100
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:02,940
And even though I am a stranger here,
they have welcomed me and supported me.

101
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:07,579
I have learned much from them, and
they have shown me so many sights.

102
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,080
I am very fond of them.

103
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,420
And that is not all.

104
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,860
I feel deeply for one of them.

105
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,680
Dare I say I love him.

106
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:21,360
And the thought of not being
able to see him now pains me so.

107
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:24,360
It feels like this
metal chest would burst.

108
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:34,760
I extend my hand in friendship
to the people of the real world,

109
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,429
and hope you will take it.

110
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:41,153
But I will not kneel to you, nor grind
my head in the dirt for your favor.

111
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:44,880
I will not, because I am human too.

112
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:49,297
I have to admit,

113
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:51,337
I never heard of the Oceanic Resource

114
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:54,017
Exploration and Research
Institute before today.

115
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:54,930
Apparently,

116
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:59,377
they were testing autonomous subs on the
Ocean Turtle when the hijacking took place.

117
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:01,677
Yes, and according to the latest reports,

118
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:06,117
the hijackers were trying to get their
hands on this AI we just heard speaking.

119
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:09,920
We also just learned a JSDF
officer was killed in the raid.

120
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:13,580
Dammit, Keeks.

121
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:17,277
I can't wrap my head around
the fact that out of all of us,

122
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:19,077
you were the one that had to die.

123
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,042
It ain't right.

124
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,350
I know.

125
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,180
It took me by surprise, too.

126
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:25,910
Oh, well.

127
00:08:25,993 --> 00:08:28,217
It's better this way
than the alternatives.

128
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:31,817
They could have either had me dragged
into court and turned into a scapegoat,

129
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:34,665
or they could have had
me disappeared for real.

130
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:38,457
But with me dead, the public's attention
is right where we want it to be.

131
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:42,422
On the bureaucrats in our government
trying to sabotage our goals.

132
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:45,857
I didn't think it went all the way up the
ladder to the Vice Minister of Defense,

133
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:46,770
though.

134
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,500
That was truly shocking.

135
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,200
No, not really.

136
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:52,177
Who needs ethics when the U .S.

137
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:54,617
weapons industry is throwing cash at you?

138
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,229
Anyway, back to your plan.

139
00:08:56,480 --> 00:09:00,197
Are you sure going public with the
AI Fluctlights was the right move?

140
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,980
I mean, by doing this,

141
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:06,629
it's totally screwing with Wrath's big
goal to use them in weaponized drones.

142
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,880
Maybe it does.

143
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,537
But now the Americans know
we have the capability,

144
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:12,796
and that, my friend, is a good thing.

145
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:15,777
Now their weapons manufacturers
can't force us to hand

146
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:18,978
over our tech under the
pretext of joint development.

147
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,497
This press conference tells the world we

148
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:24,345
perfected the AI Fluctlight
without their help.

149
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:28,774
Even if they had other plans to get
it, they won't try after seeing this.

150
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,260
Yeah, I guess not.

151
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:33,287
And we have him to thank
for getting us here.

152
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,620
Hey, Higa. Look. Look.

153
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:47,577
What? What is it?

154
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,954
Isn't the press conference over by now?

155
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:56,810
Ultimately,

156
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,537
our hope is that you'll meet artificial
Fluctlights in the virtual world,

157
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:03,460
to experience who they
are, and then, perhaps,

158
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,197
you'll change your mind.

159
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:08,740
That's all we ask of anyone
watching this broadcast today.

160
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,372
Go and see for yourself.

161
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:16,320
Uh, Doctor, that all sounds nice, but
have you considered all the possibilities?

162
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:20,346
What if they decide to, I don't
know, rise up and take us over?

163
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,294
We have considered that
possibility, but it's a stretch.

164
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:30,820
That could only happen if, say, we
tried to exterminate their kind first.

165
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:34,924
Okay, but when you think of all
the movies and books up to now...

166
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:35,937
Please excuse me.

167
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,660
I must take my leave now.

168
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,351
They're coming out of it!

169
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,310
Cait!

170
00:10:52,393 --> 00:10:53,223
Whoa, Alice!

171
00:10:53,306 --> 00:10:54,136
Careful!

172
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:06,360
How's it going, Alice?

173
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:08,120
It's been a while, huh?

174
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,700
It has.

175
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,920
Listen, it's about your little sister.

176
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:19,988
She went into deep freeze because
she wanted to wait for you.

177
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:25,980
She's up on the 80th floor of the Central
Cathedral, on that hill, sleeping.

178
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,480
Higa, I'm ready.

179
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:39,980
Dump the last 200 years from my memory.

180
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,860
Back to when the Max-Excel face kicked in.

181
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:46,480
Me and Her Highness are done there.

182
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:06,580
Yeah, come in.

183
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,030
Hey, you.

184
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:13,520
Sorry I'm so late. You're not.

185
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,520
I only woke up a second ago.

186
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:28,520
It feels to me like you're
only 90 % back to normal.

187
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:30,274
Are you eating enough?

188
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,577
Yeah, I'm eating.

189
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:33,072
I'm eating all the time.

190
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:34,530
Have some patience.

191
00:12:34,613 --> 00:12:37,364
Remember, I've been stuck
in bed for two months.

192
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:40,077
Anyway, you know when they're
letting me out of here?

193
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,480
Three days from now. Really?

194
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:45,760
Then we should celebrate
with a party or two.

195
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,740
We can have one in ALO and in real life.

196
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,400
Sounds good to me.

197
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,060
It's okay.

198
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:34,320
Deep down inside, the
memories are always there.

199
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,580
That's right, Kirito.

200
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,140
Don't cry.

201
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:41,240
Stay cool.

202
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:44,300
Yeah, you're right.

203
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:46,472
And we'll see him again.

204
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:52,820
Come on in.

205
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,270
Hey there.

206
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:56,957
A little bird told me you
were getting out soon.

207
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,780
This calls for a celebration.

208
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:01,457
Nurse Aki just told me about that,

209
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:04,017
so either you have my room
bugged or you're psychic.

210
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,982
I don't want to know either way.

211
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,110
Who cares?

212
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,717
The point is, you're doing great.

213
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:09,630
Great.

214
00:14:09,713 --> 00:14:12,497
I mean, bouncing back from a
coma after only a week of rehab?

215
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,345
Talk about the power of youth.

216
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:18,017
Now that everybody thinks you're
dead, what are you going to do?

217
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:19,747
Are you going to retire now?

218
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:24,397
We heard about what happened at Wrath,
about how they put Rank in charge.

219
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:27,068
You can't go to the
Roppongi office anymore.

220
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:28,755
Don't worry about me.

221
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:31,917
I'm still around, just
working in the background.

222
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,937
I have enough on my plate as it is,

223
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:36,717
trying to keep the Ocean
Turtle and the Underworld safe.

224
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:38,100
You are? That's great!

225
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:41,479
So do you know what'll
happen to the Underworld now?

226
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:45,016
At the moment, things aren't
looking that good for it.

227
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:48,397
The government still hasn't
picked a scapegoat to save face.

228
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:50,539
It's only a matter of time, though.

229
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:54,037
They've been itching to dismantle
Wrath, and when they do,

230
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:57,649
all our tech will get divvied
up by the major conglomerates.

231
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,360
They'll seize Alice,

232
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:03,857
then they'll probably reinitialize
the Light Cube Cluster on the Turtle.

233
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,040
But they can't!

234
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,117
You're not going to let
that happen, are you?

235
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,671
You've got a plan, right?

236
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,300
A plan?

237
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:12,500
Not really.

238
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,134
It's more like a hope.

239
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:18,077
While the government's running
around trying to save their asses,

240
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,617
I'm hoping the public
will come to acknowledge

241
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:23,465
the human rights of the
artificial Fluctlights.

242
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:27,797
And the way to achieve that is to get
as many people from the real world

243
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:32,056
as possible to have as much contact
with the Underworld as they can.

244
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:36,365
Sounds like the kind of thing the
Seed Nexus is for, doesn't it?

245
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:38,220
Yeah, I guess.

246
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:43,562
The problem is, the Underworld needs a
high-bandwidth connection to the Seed Nexus.

247
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:46,839
And the bigger the bandwidth,
the better the access.

248
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:49,937
Right now, the Underworld's
cut off from everything.

249
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:52,608
The government shut
down the Turtle Satlink.

250
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:56,557
Restoring that connection is
next on my Daddy list, in fact.

251
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:59,617
That press conference the other
day was a step toward that.

252
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:03,460
It bought us attention,
and even better, time.

253
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:05,560
The connection.

254
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:10,770
Chikuoka.

255
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,180
Please, don't let it die.

256
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,060
Please save it.

257
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:21,900
You don't have to beg me.

258
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:27,980
After all, the underworld is the
one dream I'd risk my life for, too.

259
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:42,537
It's not gonna work no
way it's gonna collapse

260
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:46,357
like always just like the
copies of me and keeks.

261
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:52,577
Did once it finds out
it's a copy there's no way

262
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:55,277
a human soul saved on a
light cube can survive.

263
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:59,197
Of the strain not even his soul

264
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:06,280
who

265
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,710
is that

266
00:17:09,793 --> 00:17:11,297
is it you Higa?

267
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:14,657
Yeah it is so you.

268
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:19,977
Didn't delete me instead
you copied and saved me.

269
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:21,017
I did.

270
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:23,337
I couldn't delete you.

271
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:28,340
You're the first Fluctlight I've
ever seen that survived 200 years.

272
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:29,497
Do you know what that means?

273
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:33,340
You're the longest living
person in human history. You!

274
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,080
I can't hit delete on that.

275
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:37,980
You get why, don't you?

276
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:45,480
I had a feeling this would happen.

277
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:49,880
Is my Fluctlight the only
one you made a copy of, Higa?

278
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:51,750
Yeah.

279
00:17:51,833 --> 00:17:53,700
Yeah, I only had time for yours.

280
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,817
During the memory delete process,
Keeks and Rank were doing other things,

281
00:17:57,900 --> 00:18:00,340
so I went ahead and copied you.

282
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:01,850
I see.

283
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:08,960
The Queen, that is Asuna.

284
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:13,065
She and I talked about
the possibility of this.

285
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:18,300
She said that if she were
the only one who got copied,

286
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:21,111
she would have herself deleted right away.

287
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:23,440
And if we both got copied,

288
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:28,308
we'd use whatever time we had left to
unite the real world and the Underworld.

289
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,940
What about if only you were copied?

290
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:33,752
Did you talk about that?

291
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,230
Yeah.

292
00:18:35,313 --> 00:18:40,060
We decided if that happened, I'd protect
the Underworld and fight only for it.

293
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:41,920
If it came to that.

294
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:45,380
What do you mean, fight?

295
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:51,060
The Underworld's fate is extremely
unstable over there, isn't it?

296
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:53,120
Yeah, it is.

297
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:57,600
The Underworld is powerless
compared to the real world.

298
00:18:57,920 --> 00:19:03,040
It relies on a power source,
hardware, maintenance, and a network.

299
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:08,297
Its existence depends on real-world
people to keep the infrastructure running.

300
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:11,760
Its safety in the long term
is precarious, at best.

301
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:15,756
You're right, but there's
just no getting around that.

302
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,057
The Light Cube Cluster?

303
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:20,717
That is the Underworld, and it
can't be moved off the Ocean Turtle.

304
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:24,094
Besides, the government's got
control of the turtle now.

305
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,760
If they wanted to, they
could cut the power tomorrow,

306
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:30,917
reinitialize the cluster,
and wipe it clean.

307
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,360
How long will the reactor's fuel last?

308
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:35,220
Um, I guess,

309
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,700
since it's a pressurized
water reactor from a sub,

310
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:42,317
and it's just powering the
cluster, then four or five years?

311
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,037
Then there's no need to
refuel during that time.

312
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:47,885
And as long as we prevent
outside interference,

313
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:51,597
The underworld will continue to
exist for that length of time.

314
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,600
Do you agree?

315
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:55,360
Yeah, but hold on a sec.

316
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:59,177
There's no weapons system on the
Turtle, and without weapons, we can't...

317
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:01,480
I said I would fight.

318
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:03,040
But how?

319
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:06,871
There's no way to connect to
the Turtle or the Cluster now.

320
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:08,917
The satellite link's been cut off.

321
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,235
There's another link.

322
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:11,640
We use that.

323
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:12,920
What link?

324
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,780
It's Heathcliff.

325
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:16,877
Akihiko Kayaba.

326
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:19,200
We need to find him right away.

327
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:22,240
You will help find him, won't you?

328
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:23,830
He...

329
00:20:23,913 --> 00:20:25,220
he's still alive?

330
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:27,510
Kayaba?

331
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:33,880
A copy of Akihiko Kayaba
and Kazuto Kirigaya.

332
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:38,880
What would happen if those copies,
I mean people, came into contact?

333
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,240
Oh my god.

334
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:44,445
I think I might have
opened Pandora's box here.

335
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:48,313
But I want to see that.

336
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:51,140
I have to know what'll happen.

337
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,520
All right, you're on.

338
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:55,517
I've got some old contacts.

339
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:56,953
I'll send a few emails.

340
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:58,595
Encrypted, of course.

341
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:27,100
You can take a nap after you finish
doing your sacred arts homework.

342
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:30,020
No, you can't copy mine.

343
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:36,117
Hey, I tweaked that skill
you taught me the other day,

344
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,857
let's go to the training
hall so I can show you.

345
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:40,577
I knew it.

346
00:21:40,660 --> 00:21:42,457
You snuck out to buy snacks again.

347
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:45,297
I hope you got some for me this time.

348
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:48,240
Come on, Kirito. Wake up.

349
00:21:50,060 --> 00:21:50,890
Kirito.

350
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:07,260
I should have had all my memories in
that place to lead it. Everything.

351
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:10,360
Especially the time I spent on YouTube.

352
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:28,120
Hey, tell me about it,

353
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:34,000
all the fun things and the sad
things, from the beginning to the end.

354
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:43,100
When I met him, who's
walking through a forest?

355
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,360
Yu-Gi-Oh was chopping at a tree.

356
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:50,500
He was a woodcutter in the underworld.

357
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:53,740
His job was to cut down this big cedar.

358
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:58,340
A tree that, for 300 years,
couldn't be cut down by anyone.

359
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:17,770
Kirito...

360
00:23:17,853 --> 00:23:20,157
I feel...

361
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:24,500
I feel like I might die.

362
00:23:36,220 --> 00:23:38,300
Next, New World.
